f", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "653b11bb-8c95-447c-adfa-57cf9cbf718b", "type": "concept", "title": "colonial archive"}, {"id": "95be350c-ae3c-4969-bcec-cbeecfbeed7c", "type": "concept", "title": "missionary ethnography"}, {"id": "2c823e68-95d6-4ac6-a22f-c63d1dd6da1f", "type": "concept", "title": "census categories"}, {"id": "114cbcc0-2c32-4c3d-8e1a-65e7b57c8315", "type": "concept", "title": "tribe/caste/religion"}, {"id": "93fae045-bcc8-4e89-9c4a-b1123870d662", "type": "concept", "title": "conversion"}, {"id": "18b43a1b-f6fa-497a-ae86-02ebe703e4f0", "type": "concept", "title": "indirect rule"}, {"id": "f254c43b-e4e8-4e4f-a317-0281857bfe05", "type": "concept", "title": "legal codification"}, {"id": "daf1d1cf-c00d-4d68-824f-20e7e0187a97", "type": "concept", "title": "ethnological display"}, {"id": "285e24a9-1dff-438f-9e67-11d65f74e8fb", "type": "concept", "title": "salvage anthropology"}, {"id": "d277eeaa-04d9-4db8-b0c6-49420aecbb52", "type": "concept", "title": "knowledge/power"}], "description": "Students examine how administrators, missionaries, museums, and scholars classified traditions under imperial rule."}, {"id": "6f7aff07-e7c1-43d6-b7b6-9a156aaed1f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Orientalism and representation", "children": [{"id": "2fd2d132-dc15-4eb8-ac8a-910c255d52de", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "4907f317-3f0b-491d-9fe9-123d287bd649", "type": "concept", "title": "Orientalism"}, {"id": "57bfc13f-eccd-476c-9de4-f93dd15b5edc", "type": "concept", "title": "exoticism"}, {"id": "8d69e7ff-ba71-439b-8a5e-215a673e80d3", "type": "concept", "title": "essentialism"}, {"id": "308aeccb-b8df-4a0f-9f26-380fd3efa891", "type": "concept", "title": "othering"}, {"id": "fbeb5d3f-0366-4f1b-88b9-0fce2cf1b618", "type": "concept", "title": "civilizational discourse"}, {"id": "0d32b136-b060-4ecd-8623-a7e8ebe2af2a", "type": "concept", "title": "racialization"}, {"id": "cf2a1e08-da80-4397-a553-0b94ea2a6aa2