": "Students learn to analyze religion in violence and peacebuilding without assuming religion is either uniquely violent or inherently peaceful."}]}, {"id": "3c53e8e3-0a08-4d9f-bc41-faee5aef3bfe", "type": "topic", "title": "Secularism, Secularization, Nonreligion, and Spirituality", "description": "This unit treats the secular and nonreligion as objects of study. Students learn that secularity is historically made, politically contested, and culturally varied.", "children": [{"id": "7bf0a1cc-229a-4e85-950f-ccbb41e34af1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Secularism as formation", "children": [{"id": "cf1375cf-dbfb-4881-8bb2-79b5567206ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "4618dba5-1cb7-4a1f-a7b0-da11e8519422", "type": "concept", "title": "secular"}, {"id": "a488418a-d2af-4b1a-9f74-7f748869202a", "type": "concept", "title": "secularism"}, {"id": "ef8b598e-22dc-4b86-9fc1-431b118b949b", "type": "concept", "title": "secularity"}, {"id": "e665a6b2-be95-4827-8b1a-b87c3ded7c7f", "type": "concept", "title": "differentiation"}, {"id": "dd99a419-8233-46f9-98fe-6e58300c1d6b", "type": "concept", "title": "privatization"}, {"id": "d69c7aef-a1d3-48f2-95de-626226b84ca0", "type": "concept", "title": "public/private boundary"}, {"id": "9f9121e4-3d61-463f-ac44-0b1a3db115ae", "type": "concept", "title": "neutrality claim"}, {"id": "056b9873-0b14-404e-a87b-82d295243bd2", "type": "concept", "title": "religion-making"}, {"id": "1847ddd1-eb24-4207-8a88-52f33289bc88", "type": "concept", "title": "modernity"}, {"id": "75f8fd4a-1f22-4d13-bedf-f6d6ce222c40", "type": "concept", "title": "postsecular"}], "description": "Students distinguish secularization as a social process from secularism as a political and cultural project."}, {"id": "412472bd-fb96-4f79-a152-bae56a1ab0df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonreligion and unbelief", "children": [{"id": "a3453f00-36f6-4796-a120-cbce10d20e92", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "05e54072-8a84-452c-a917-3eb1b159fe63", "type": "concept", "title": "atheism"}, {"id": "26acbe05-3275-4073-b435-8dcf391c9f31", "type": "concept", "title": "agnosticism"}, {"id": "2bd17a8c-a3a2-450c-8bb9-5b11c429d8af", "type": "concept", "title": "humanism"}, {"id": "c298845f-c9a9-4018-a6bd-70782e1909ba", "type": "concept", "title": "religious none"}, {"id": "40a744a5-5680-4276-994a-0047cb87d2d5", "type": "concept", "title": "indifference"}, {"id": "dc9bbc44-7f2b-4c14-a980-db2b3451dcbe", "type": "concept", "title": "deconversion"}, {"id": "6f8afed7-0461-4b10-85b1-144ebf4d7483", "type": "concept", "title": "apostasy"}, {"id": "fcb56832-b1a4-4045-a166-2e91a57fcfae", "type": "concept", "title": "skepticism"}, {"id": "524bb391-b787-4956-aabc-395a3e9bc28b", "type": "concept", "title": "freethought"}, {"id": "c940a838-7766-4a17-a5d2-7c42bbfc1403", "type": "concept", "title": "secular community"}], "description": "This subtopic studies atheism, agnosticism, humanism, indifference, and the category of the religious none."}, {"id": "b26faca7-5937-46c8-af51-f65b3a996ef5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spirituality and lived alternatives", "children": [{"id": "085c7241-a073-4b3d-9edf-9b5c68e54946", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "f24ce665-eb46-4e42-9585-ad7b280c2bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "spiritual but not religious"}, {"id": "c30ed841-6752-48df-bcfb-07abdaff03e8", "type": "concept", "title": "wellness culture"}, {"id": "755acf28-7f00-4953-be11-5ddc7c4d0677", "type": "concept", "title": "new age"}, {"id": "0b95796b-ea75-43e6-a86f-46171a2142af", "type": "concept", "title": "mindfulness"}, {"id": "8aef9f6d-27e5-494e-bb18-44edc7cacc8d", "type": "concept", "title": "enchantment"}, {"id": "4aaed40e-f0e2-40fb-9ed5-d7dafbdb90ba", "type": "concept", "title": "holism"}, {"id": "f0970dab-5302-4ac9-bc72-50c583134abb", "type": "concept", "title": "therapeutic culture"}, {"id": "5b97225b-5c0d-4b3c-9001-94ea52d2a350", "type": "concept", "title": "hybridity"}, {"id": "a5ec12ea-e6f1-461a-a9af-aea367a2cfcb", "type": "concept", "title": "consumer spirituality"}, {"id": "4e306983-1537-408a-9b69-3a11107dd769", "type": "concept", "title": "personal practice"}], "description": "Students examine spirituality, wellness, new age practices, enchantment, and hybrid identities without treating them as less serious than institutional religion."}]}, {"id": "728b943d-d3a8-4c58-8c70-1f8371743305", "type": "topic", "title": "Media, Digital Religion, Popular Culture, and Technology", "description": "This unit studies how religion circulates through print, broadcast, social media, platforms, games, algorithms, and online communities.", "children": [{"id": "25b1af25-135e-4816-abd6-103e6052d3a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mediation and authority", "children": [{"id": "1a104ccd-e012-4584-84f2-279164570c8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "5e262de1-09c3-4642-9c73-7c4ff1ef8af7", "type": "concept", "title": "mediation"}, {"id": "59ecf60a-152d-4ae3-9b44-a88b50d4f3d9", "type": "concept", "title": "media ecology"}, {"id": "c5b1347b-d480-40a5-ab1e-559753b7ea32", "type": "concept", "title": "broadcast religion"}, {"id": "51ded332-e382-4182-9dda-184cd98ec6ca", "type": "concept", "title": "televangelism"}, {"id": "d6acac0e-0e36-4650-9b75-9fe672ae23c1", "type": "concept", "title": "print publics"}, {"id": "00040db0-6b3d-4898-b06e-abd788fd3410", "type": "concept", "title": "algorithmic visibility"}, {"id": "ed135824-9759-4654-bcf4-4ca07e1f90f4", "type": "concept", "title": "platform authority"}, {"id": "564c0047-8f13-49de-aa7a-c16b13dc777d", "type": "concept", "title": "authenticity"}, {"id": "5c397d87-5327-4cd2-b829-f3c2d1159bf4", "type": "concept", "title": "parasocial authority"}, {"id": "e7f3b90a-de26-4738-8003-ea2ec0bda378", "type": "concept", "title": "networked publics"}], "description": "Students analyze how media technologies reshape religious authority, authenticity, access, and community boundaries."}, {"