pe": "concept", "title": "controlled comparison"}, {"id": "c828cea1-f541-447a-8640-171a11fa5ef3", "type": "concept", "title": "asymmetrical comparison"}, {"id": "ad2d6022-46f6-48ea-bc58-807fda9214cd", "type": "concept", "title": "genealogy"}, {"id": "a1f638de-d70d-43bf-a48d-65850830088c", "type": "concept", "title": "family resemblance"}, {"id": "1607d03c-6349-4b67-b6a9-02d35ccef182", "type": "concept", "title": "contrast class"}, {"id": "5a724a11-d364-4bc0-94c2-2adf9f0d8e9c", "type": "concept", "title": "third term"}, {"id": "81568998-9e2c-48cc-b1a2-2c32d2785490", "type": "concept", "title": "methodological transparency"}, {"id": "f6babb32-47ae-48c6-8eb6-1594c0cf2de9", "type": "concept", "title": "overgeneralization"}], "description": "Students practice designing comparisons that clarify difference, avoid ranking, and state the analytic purpose clearly."}]}, {"id": "3eb34fcd-c698-4960-a42c-26c7acae0c71", "type": "topic", "title": "Research Design, Ethics, Fieldwork, Archives, and Data Practices", "description": "This unit turns theory into research craft. Students learn how to build a feasible, ethical project with clear questions, evidence, methods, and limitations.", "children": [{"id": "c363927c-20be-4ace-9ba9-ab9bcdab9246", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research questions and design", "children": [{"id": "ce4725b0-3de1-4cca-b3fc-f2929eaaf198", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "523d8489-e864-4096-801b-6c2a87c63c74", "type": "concept", "title": "research question"}, {"id": "f9644d8e-8474-4453-b98b-a3e06f38bf26", "type": "concept", "title": "scope"}, {"id": "64f9c732-3205-427b-ac48-680727e65a72", "type": "concept", "title": "case selection"}, {"id": "fcec5ece-07d2-441b-b716-96d5a72400d5", "type": "concept", "title": "literature review"}, {"id": "2b13ed49-130d-473c-bb17-5d4262cddfc7", "type": "concept", "title": "method alignment"}, {"id": "1f215932-0f3f-483c-b403-fb1b95e79bda", "type": "concept", "title": "hypothesis versus interpr